                     /synonym="cat promoter"
                     /note="Promoter of the Tn9 cat gene, taken from V00622
                     (Alton and Vapnek 1979) 140-217. Both ends are provisional:
                     no accessible source maps its transcription start, -35 or
                     -10. The 3' end leaves 26 bases before the cat start codon
                     (V00622 218-243), outside the Shine-Dalgarno region and the
                     catalog part RBS 23400; the 103 bp this part carried before
                     ran to the ATG and overlapped RBS 23400 on 228 plasmids of
                     a 1,390-plasmid collection. Where the -35 and -10 lie is an
                     open question, and the part declares no boxes until a
                     source settles it. Two readings fit a 17 bp spacer. (A)
                     TTGATC at 1-6 (V00622 140-145, which is why the window
                     starts there) with AACTTT at 24-29 (V00622 163-168): this
                     -10 ends 22 bp before the IS10 target TACCGGGCG at 52-60,
                     the distance Gonzalez-Prieto et al. 2015 report between the
                     promoter's -10 element and that target, but it matches the
                     -10 consensus TATAAT at only 2 of 6 bases. (B) ACGTAA at
                     10-15 with CATAAT at 33-38 (V00622 172-177): the better -10
                     match (5 of 6) and the pair older automated annotations
                     mark on cat-carrying vectors, but it ends 13 bp before the
                     target, not 22. Positions are 1-based in the part."
                     /citation=[1]
                     /citation=[2]
                     /db_xref="SO:0000167"
